> sending the "X" system message doesn't have much of an effect! 

I doubt Link even looks at such information.

> Anyone know how to tell an IMG process to stop?

You need to send it a 'terminate' message.  This won't always stop it, 
but it is better than a straight 'Kill', which is supposed to be a last 
resort.

Heres some code which should stop the link, given its Process ID and a 
reason for its demise.  The reason can be zero.

PROC term:(pid%,reason%)
LOCAL ax%,bx%,cx%,dx%,si%,di% REM must be in this order
LOCAL flags%

bx%=pid%
ax%=$0D00 REM AH=0x0d for terminate, 0x08 for kill
ax%=ax% OR (Reason% AND $00FF)
flags%=OS($88,addr(ax%))  :REM $88 for PROCMANAGER
flags%=flags% AND $0001
return(flags%)
ENDP

Please forgive me if it doesn't work, it's simply a reworked version of 
the OS call example code as in the programming guide.



